//? Title: Log-Link GLMs: Means, Likelihoods and Scores
//? Subtitle: Poisson, gamma and negative-binomial likelihoods imply different variance models
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Positive means can describe integer counts or strictly positive measurements, but one mean
function does not determine a response distribution. We compare three log-link likelihoods at
hand-checkable observations and verify autograd against their analytic scores. Shape and size
are fixed here, keeping mean estimation separate from dispersion estimation.
)
\toc

> The method

All three families use eta=Xw and mu=exp(eta). Poisson has variance mu; gamma with known shape
a has variance mu²/a; negative binomial with known size r has variance mu+mu²/r. Their derivatives
of per-observation negative log likelihood with respect to eta are

$$
\partial_\eta\ell_{\rm Pois}=\mu-y,\quad
\partial_\eta\ell_{\rm Gamma}=a(1-y/\mu),\quad
\partial_\eta\ell_{\rm NB}=\frac{r(\mu-y)}{r+\mu}.
$$
\alttext(The Poisson, gamma and negative-binomial score residuals differ in how they weight the same observed-minus-mean discrepancy.)

These follow by differentiating the distribution log densities after substituting mu=exp(eta).
The coefficient gradient is Xᵀ times these scores. GlmNll retains response normalising constants
in the reported likelihood while stopping their response gradients. Gamma requires y>0; count
families use nonnegative integer y. Callers supply valid response support and finite predictors.
The helper is a log-link likelihood, including for gamma; it differs from stats::GLM's inverse-link
gamma family. NB uses a softplus expression for stability. Shape/size are supplied, not estimated.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/generalized_linear_models_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/generalized_linear_models_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/generalized_linear_models_concept.tikz > build/generalized_linear_models_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/generalized_linear_models_concept.svg build/generalized_linear_models_concept.dvi > build/generalized_linear_models_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/generalized_linear_models_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
