> Simple examples

At eta=0 and y=2, mu=1. Scores are -1 for Poisson, -3 for gamma shape 3 and -2/3 for negative-binomial size 2.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/generalized_linear_models_scores.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::ml;
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame t;
  std::vector<std::string> family;
  std::vector<double> nll, score, exact;
  int i = 0;
  for (auto f :
       {m::GlmFamily::kPoisson, m::GlmFamily::kGamma, m::GlmFamily::kNegativeBinomial}) {
    auto eta = n::scalar(0, n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_();
    const auto loss = m::GlmNll(eta, n::scalar(2, n::DType::Float64), f, i == 1 ? 3 : 2);
    const double g = n::grad(loss, {eta})[0].item(), e = i == 0 ? -1 : i == 1 ? -3 : -2. / 3;
    if (std::abs(g - e) > 1e-12)
      return 1;
    family.push_back(i == 0 ? "Poisson" : i == 1 ? "gamma shape 3" : "NB size 2");
    nll.push_back(loss.item());
    score.push_back(g);
    exact.push_back(e);
    ++i;
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.bars({0, 1, 2}, score, "score in eta", {37, 99, 235}, .5)
      .title("Same mean and response, different score weights")
      .x_label("Poisson=0, gamma=1, NB=2")
      .y_label("NLL derivative");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  p.y_limits(-3.4, .25).size(850, 420).save_svg("build/generalized_linear_models_scores.svg");
  t.add_column("family", family);
  t.add_column("NLL", nll);
  t.add_column("autograd_score", score);
  t.add_column("analytic_score", exact);
  std::print("{}\n", t.to_md(8));
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| family | NLL | autograd_score | analytic_score |
| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Poisson | 1.69314718 | -1.00000000 | -1.00000000 |
| gamma shape 3 | 2.01101595 | -3.00000000 | -3.00000000 |
| NB size 2 | 1.90954250 | -0.66666667 | -0.66666667 |

\image(figures/generalized_linear_models_scores.svg)
// result_end
